// The FALSE-REFUSAL CONTROL for `scripts/stale-binary-gate.sh` CHECK 5, and its only job.
//
// ⭐ THE GATE REFUSES TO RUN A SUITE ON A COMPILER OLDER THAN ITS OWN SOURCES, and a refusal it
// cannot justify wedges the suite exactly as thoroughly as a stale binary lies to it. So the gate
// needs one source that IS under the project root and is NOT compiled into the binary — ageing this
// file forward must change no verdict. The `.maxonignore` beside it is what excludes it, so the
// subtree is the whole fixture and nothing here may be reached from `maxon-bin/Main.maxon`.
//
// ⚠ IT IS A DEDICATED FIXTURE RATHER THAN A BORROWED PROGRAM. A control that shares a file with
// something else stops being a control the moment that something else is moved or deleted, and the
// gate would then pass by testing nothing.

function main() returns ExitCode
	return 0
end 'main'
